\section{Results and pagination}{

\code{select()} returns one page, which the server can limit further. Use
\code{limit}, \code{offset} and a stable \code{order} to fetch more. Set \code{count} to
\code{"exact"}, \code{"planned"} or \code{"estimated"} to request a total.

Use \code{raw = TRUE} for an httr2 response and inspect its Content-Range with
\code{httr2::resp_header()}. Otherwise selections return data frames, with
large integers preserved as strings. Embedded resources can produce
nested data frames or list columns. Empty selections have no column
metadata. Dates and decimal strings keep their JSON representation.
